annotations:
- name: annotate1
  mode: annotate
  title: APC mini MIDI -> hydra page
  text: midiin_apc reads the APC mini mk2 (device id 1 in Dialogs > MIDI Device Mapper, 0-based CC numbers). midi_to_web pushes every changed channel into the hydra page in webrender1 via executeJavaScript -> midi.set(); the sketch reads cc(n) / note(n). Faders = CC 48-56, pads = notes 0-63.
  position: [-745, 322]
  size: [770, 274]
  color: [0.35, 0.5, 0.2]
- name: annotate2
  mode: annotate
  title: Group 1 (red screens)
  text: 3 rectangles from mockup screens.svg, merged with a unique group per input. Sizes and positions are expressions on ScreenMap's layout table (op.ScreenMap.Layout) -- edit the screens table or drag in ScreenMap/editor, not these parameters.
  position: [1075, 850]
  size: [670, 406]
  color: [0.45, 0.2, 0.2]
- name: annotate3
  mode: annotate
  title: Group 2 (green screens)
  text: 3 rectangles, two are the 90-degree rotated ones (width/height swapped). Sizes and positions are expressions on ScreenMap's layout table (op.ScreenMap.Layout) -- edit the screens table or drag in ScreenMap/editor, not these parameters.
  position: [1075, 355]
  size: [670, 428]
  color: [0.2, 0.45, 0.2]
- name: annotate4
  mode: annotate
  title: Group 3 (blue screens)
  text: 3 rectangles, one rotated. Sizes and positions are expressions on ScreenMap's layout table (op.ScreenMap.Layout) -- edit the screens table or drag in ScreenMap/editor, not these parameters.
  position: [1075, -71]
  size: [670, 390]
  color: [0.2, 0.25, 0.5]
- name: annotate5
  mode: annotate
  title: Unique screens (black)
  text: 7 single rectangles, merged with a unique group per input. Sizes and positions are expressions on ScreenMap's layout table (op.ScreenMap.Layout) -- edit the screens table or drag in ScreenMap/editor, not these parameters.
  position: [1075, -1000]
  size: [670, 893]
  color: [0.3, 0.3, 0.3]
- name: annotate6
  mode: annotate
  title: Preset 1 -> group 1 screens
  text: crop_pane1 takes the top third of webrender1 (preset 1, 1280x720). Group 1's bounding box is fitted into that pane at one scale (3.79 px per svg px, centred), and crop_g1_01..03 cut each red screen's own window out of it, so every crop has its screen's aspect ratio and content runs continuously across the three screens. Each crop textures its rectangle through mat_g1_xx / geo_g1_xx; cam_ortho (width 4.85 = the sheet) and render_g1 (1280x602) show the result.
  position: [2830, 21]
  size: [1870, 1266]
  color: [0.45, 0.2, 0.2]
- name: annotate7
  mode: annotate
  title: Preset 2 -> group 2 screens
  text: crop_pane2 = middle third of webrender1 (preset 2). Group 2's bounding box fitted into the pane at 4.0 px per svg px, centred; crop_g2_01..03 cut each green screen's window (two are the rotated screens, portrait crops). select_g2_01..03 pull each screen's rectangle (rect_g2_xx) by reference, mat_g2_xx / geo_g2_xx texture them; render1 uses the shared cameraViewport.
  position: [2830, -2070]
  size: [1870, 1170]
  color: [0.2, 0.45, 0.2]
- name: annotate8
  mode: annotate
  title: Preset 3 -> group 3 screens
  text: crop_pane3 = bottom third of webrender1 (preset 3). Group 3's bounding box fitted at 3.99 px per svg px, centred; crop_g3_01..03 cut each blue screen's window (03 is the rotated one). select_g3_01..03 pull each screen's rectangle (rect_g3_xx) by reference, mat_g3_xx / geo_g3_xx texture them; render1 uses the shared cameraViewport.
  position: [2830, -3670]
  size: [1870, 1170]
  color: [0.2, 0.25, 0.5]
- name: annotate9
  mode: annotate
  title: Rendered clips -> non-interactive screens
  text: The 7 small screens play pre-rendered clips instead of live hydra. All 60 clips (320x180, 600 frames each, rendered offline by Hydra/tools/render-clips.mjs) are joined into ONE HAP movie, Hydra/clips-all.mov, in the order listed by clip_list (Hydra/clips-all.txt). movie_u01..07 all read that file with Specify Index; each index = its clip_state row's start + frames since t0, looped over 600. clip_switcher (Execute DAT, frame start) swaps ONE random screen every random 5..10 s to a clip not already playing (never the same screen twice in a row) by rewriting its clip_state row -- no file is opened or closed at runtime (swapping PNG-sequence folders crashed TD on the Mac after 1-2 h). crop_u01..07 centre-crop the 320x180 clip to that screen's aspect in whole pixels (nearest filtering); select_u01..07 pull each screen's rectangle (rect_unique_xx) by reference, mat_uxx / geo_uxx texture them. window_u01..07 (Window COMPs, closed until opened) output each crop_u0N to the display and pixel size given in ScreenMap's screens table; a 0 px size falls back to the crop's own resolution.
  position: [2830, -7450]
  size: [1870, 3350]
  color: [0.3, 0.3, 0.3]
